        "abstract": "We design and optimize two non-standard dosimeter circuits: an Active Pixel Sensor and a Floating Gate Sensor, for fabrication on a standard CMOS process. An Active Pixel Sensor is found suitable for dose rates down to 3.6 mGy s<sup xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">−1</sup>, with a sensitivity of 7.1 V Gy<sup xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">−1</sup>. A Floating Gate dosimeter is optimized for a sensitivity of 46mV Gy<sup xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">−1</sup>, with a noise-equivalent dose of 0.2mGy.",
